1. Work performed

Updated [attention_layer.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/attention_layer.cpp) so `AttentionLayerSlice::Impl` now owns persistent single-token BF16 attention buffers for:
- `query_bf16`
- `attn_output_bf16`

They are allocated at `Create()` time with the decode shape `[1, query_head_count, 1, head_dim]`, and `Run()` now reuses them when `token_count == 1 && NEMOTRON_FORWARD_DECODE_SCRATCH` is enabled. The existing per-call allocation path remains in place for `token_count > 1`.

